# Keep .mjs checkouts LF everywhere: vitest (esbuild) fails to parse CRLF
# .mjs files on Windows ("SyntaxError: Invalid or unexpected token" when a
# test imports a sync script), which core.autocrlf=true would otherwise
# produce. Blobs are already LF, so this changes checkouts only, not history.
*.mjs text eol=lf

# The generated vault (*.generated.ts) is written LF by the sync scripts;
# pin LF so the check:generated guard never sees spurious CRLF diffs.
*.generated.ts text eol=lf

# Shell scripts run directly via their shebang on GitHub Actions' Linux
# runners (scripts/watchdog/upsert-alert.sh) — a CRLF checkout breaks the
# shebang line ("bad interpreter") even though core.autocrlf only converts
# working-tree checkouts, not the committed blob. Same risk class as the
# .mjs fix above; pin explicitly rather than rely on autocrlf leaving it
# alone by chance.
*.sh text eol=lf

# AI Dev OS writes .claude/rules/*.md with LF and compares the checked-out
# file byte-for-byte against its packaged copy (src/team/bootstrap.mjs). Under
# core.autocrlf=true a CRLF checkout is content-identical but never byte-equal,
# so `ai-dev team-status` reports "up to date: false" forever and invites
# someone to re-run bootstrap or hand-edit a file the docs say not to touch.
# Pin LF so the comparison stays meaningful.
.claude/rules/*.md text eol=lf
